--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PanelAero -- doublet-lattice aerodynamics
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The `dlm` aerodynamic backend of Flutter Calculator does not implement the
doublet-lattice method itself. It builds a panel mesh and a modal downwash,
calls PanelAero to obtain the unsteady aerodynamic influence coefficients Qjj,
and projects the resulting pressures onto the Rayleigh-Ritz modes. All of the
unsteady-kernel mathematics is PanelAero's work.

    Project:  PanelAero
    Authors:  Deutsches Zentrum fuer Luft- und Raumfahrt e.V. (DLR),
              Institute of Aeroelasticity
    Source:   https://github.com/DLR-AE/PanelAero
    Licence:  BSD 3-Clause (reproduced in full below)

PanelAero is a separate package, installed from its own upstream source; no part
of it is copied into this repository. It is required only for the `dlm` backend
-- the analytic `theodorsen` backend does not use it.

The DLR is named here solely to identify the authors of software this project
depends on. This is a statement of provenance: the DLR neither endorses nor is
affiliated with Flutter Calculator, in keeping with clause 3 below.

If your work uses results produced through this backend, please also cite
PanelAero's own recommended reference, given in the repository linked above.

